questions.explanation:
The Common Mode Rejection Ratio (CMRR) is \[\mathrm{CMRR}=\frac{A_{d}}{A_{cm}}\] Given, \[A_{d}=10^{5}, \qquad
A_{cm}=0.01=10^{-2}\] Hence, \[\mathrm{CMRR}
=\frac{10^{5}}{10^{-2}}
=10^{7}\] CMRR in decibels is \[\mathrm{CMRR}_{dB}
=20\log_{10}(\mathrm{CMRR})\] \[=20\log_{10}(10^{7})
=20\times7
=140\,\text{dB}\] \[\boxed{140}\]
